  "id": "emotional-valence",
  "term": "emotional valence",
  "definition": "Emotional valence is the emotional quality of a stimulus or experience in terms of whether it is positive, neutral, or negative. In cognition, it is used to describe an emotional factor that can influence processes such as attention and memory.",
